          "examStrategy": "This unit asks you to do something the DU syllabus has now made explicit: take Indian jurisprudence seriously as jurisprudence — as Parasain says, to \"relocate the Indian mind in Indian thought\" without parroting Western methods, but also without uncritical revivalism; to show, with Dhyani, that the ancient order was \"a government of laws and not of men\", that the king was under law, that the judge was independent and accountable; and, with Seema Singh & Yadav, that the indigenous dispute-resolution tradition is not dead but institutionalised — Art 40, the 73rd Amendment, the Fifth and Sixth Schedules, Lok Adalats, the Mediation Act, 2023, and the courts' own acceptance of panchayat awards in Vytla Sitanna. Learn the texts, learn the cases, learn the four distinctions of East and West — and write with the confidence that your answer is built on the University's own material.",
