          "arguments": "<p><b>Appellant:</b> Cadet taking an IAF aircraft on an unauthorised flight to Pakistan was an operational breach of discipline, not theft, as there was no intention to permanently retain the government plane.</p><p><b>Respondent (State):</b> Taking military aircraft out of possession without authority for personal advantage causes wrongful gain to the cadet and wrongful loss to the State.</p>",
          "principleEvolved": "<p><b>Dishonest Intention in Theft:</b> (1) 'Dishonest intention' under BNS Section 2(7) / IPC Section 24 exists when an act causes wrongful gain or wrongful loss. (2) Unauthorised temporary taking of property for personal use constitutes theft, even if the offender intended to return it subsequently.</p>"
