          "examStrategy": "(1) Bigamy: converting to Islam does NOT dissolve an existing Hindu marriage; second marriage is void and bigamous under IPC § 494 (Sarla Mudgal, Lily Thomas). (2) Distinguish Void marriages (S. 11: no legal status, no decree needed) from Voidable marriages (S. 12: valid until annulled by decree).",
          "caseMap": "1. Bhaurao (1965) · 2. Sarla Mudgal (1995) · 3. Lily Thomas (2000) · 4. Seema v. Ashwani Kumar (2006).",
          "htmlContent": "<div class=\"sec\" id=\"rev\">\n<div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-no\">11</div><div><h2>One-Page Revision — Tables, Mnemonics, Final Flowcharts<small>LAST-NIGHT + MORNING-OF-EXAM • 20 MINUTES</small></h2></div></div>\n\n<h3>11.1 Mnemonics (mug in 2 min)</h3>\n<div class=\"kv\">\n<div class=\"kcard\"><b>Sec 5: “My Mental Age Prohibits Sapinda”</b><br><b>M</b>onogamy (i)→Void<br><b>M</b>ental (ii)→Voidable<br><b>A</b>ge (iii)→Valid+Punish<br><b>P</b>rohibited (iv)→Void<br><b>S</b>apinda (v)→Void<br>→ <b>“3 Void (i,iv,v) • 1 Voidable (ii) • 1 Valid (iii)”</b></div>\n<div class=\"kcard\"><b>Sec 12: “I Married Fraudulent Pregnant”</b><br><b>I</b>mpotency (a)<br><b>M</b>ental 5(ii) (b)<br><b>F</b>raud/Force (c)<br><b>P</b>regnant by other (d)<br>Bars: <b>C+D = 1-year clock</b></div>\n<div class=\"kcard\"><b>Bigamy proof: “FSS”</b><br><b>F</b>irst valid<br><b>S</b>ubsisting<br><b>S</b>olemnized second<br>+ Void under 17 = ingredient<br><i>Lokhande (No) vs Nagalingam (Yes)</i></div>\n<div class=\"kcard\"><b>Custom proof: “ACRUP”</b><br><b>A</b>ncient <b>C</b>ertain <b>R</b>easonable <b>U</b>niform <b>P</b>ublic-policy-ok<br>+ Plead + Clear evidence<br>Strict construction (<i>Surajmani</i>)</div>\n</div>\n\n<h3>11.2 Ultimate Distinction Table (photocopy in mind)</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Question</th><th>Void Sec 11</th><th>Voidable Sec 12</th><th>Valid-but-punishable (Age)</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Sections</td><td>5(i)(iv)(v)</td><td>12(a)(b)(c)(d)</td><td>5(iii) + PCMA 3/12/14</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Status</td><td>Ab initio, ipso jure</td><td>Valid till decree</td><td>Valid; voidable at child’s option (PCMA)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Petition</td><td>Either party, no limit</td><td>Aggrieved, 1-yr bars (c)(d)</td><td>Child within 2 yrs of majority (PCMA)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Punishment</td><td>17/494/495 + 18(b)</td><td>None</td><td>18(a) 2 yrs/₹1L + PCMA 9–11</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Children</td><td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center\">Legitimate Sec 16 (property: parents only — Bharatha Matha)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Lead cases</td><td>Lily, Nagalingam, Lokhande</td><td>P. v. K., Babui, Asha</td><td>Pinninti, Lajja</td></tr></table>\n\n<h3>11.3 Final Master Flowchart — Every Validity Problem</h3>\n<div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"fchart\">\n<div class=\"fbox gold\"><b>STEP 1: Sec 2 — Two Hindus? Domiciled? Not ST? (Surajmani) — If no → HMA out (SMA/custom)</b></div><div class=\"farrow\">⬇</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\"><b>STEP 2: Sec 5(i) Monogamy? (Lily) → Sec 5(iv) Prohibited 3(g)? → Sec 5(v) Sapinda 3(f)? → Sec 5(ii) Mental? → Sec 5(iii) Age?</b></div><div class=\"farrow\">⬇</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\"><b>STEP 3: Sec 7 Solemnized? (homa/saptapadi or 7-A or custom — Lokhande/Nagalingam) → Sec 8 Registration only proof (Seema)</b></div><div class=\"farrow\">⬇</div>\n<div class=\"frow\"><div class=\"fbox\" style=\"border-color:#7b1e1e\"><b>Void 11?</b><br>(i)/(iv)/(v)<br>+ 17/494/495</div><div class=\"fbox\" style=\"border-color:#b45309\"><b>Voidable 12?</b><br>(a)-(d) + bars<br>needs decree</div><div class=\"fbox green\"><b>Age valid?</b><br>Pinninti + PCMA<br>Lajja option</div></div><div class=\"farrow\">⬇</div>\n<div class=\"fbox gold\"><b>STEP 4: Sec 16 Legitimacy + Sec 18 Punishment + Sec 114 Presumption / Live-in protection (Velusamy) + Conclusion</b></div>\n</div></div>\n\n<h3>11.4 10-Case One-Line Recall (write 1 line per case in exam)</h3>\n<table><tr><th>#</th><th>Case</th><th>One-line ratio (mug)</th></tr>\n<tr><td>1</td><td>Surajmani AIR 2001 SC 938</td><td>STs outside HMA; custom strictly proved; custom ≠ offence.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2</td><td>Nagalingam (2001) 7 SCC 487</td><td>TN 7-A thali/garlands = valid; saptapadi only if admitted essential → bigamy.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3</td><td>Lokhande AIR 1965 SC 1564</td><td>No homa/saptapadi + no custom = not solemnized → no 494.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4</td><td>Lily Thomas AIR 2000 SC 1650</td><td>Feigned conversion ≠ dissolution; M2 void + 494; Art 20/25 fail.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5</td><td>Pinninti AIR 1977 AP 43 (FB)</td><td>5(iii) age → valid, neither void nor voidable; only 18 + 13(2)(iv).</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6</td><td>Asha Qureshi AIR 2002 MP 263</td><td>Concealed widowhood = fraud (duty to speak) → nullity SMA 25(iii) ≈ 12(1)(c).</td></tr>\n<tr><td>7</td><td>Lajja 2012 (193) DLT 61 (FB)</td><td>HMA valid + PCMA voidable at child’s option; husband ≠ guardian; no auto-quash.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8</td><td>P. v. K. AIR 1982 Bom 400</td><td>Prolapse concealment = impotency + material fraud → annulment (a)+(c).</td></tr>\n<tr><td>9</td><td>Babui Panmato AIR 1968 Pat 190</td><td>60 as 25–30 via mother-agent + veil = fraud; pre-marriage fraud suffices.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10</td><td>Seema (2006) 2 SCC 578</td><td>Registration = rebuttable presumption, not validity; all religions compulsory.</td></tr></table>\n\n<div class=\"imp\"><b>⚠️ Last-minute warnings (examiners deduct for these):</b> (1) Never call age-violation “void” under HMA — say valid + PCMA voidable. (2) Never say live-in = marriage — say protected but not status. (3) Never say registration = validity — say proof. (4) Never say conversion dissolves — say ground for divorce only. (5) Never say second wife has no rights — say no HMA status but 125/DV purposive (Badshah). (6) Always mention Sec 16 legitimacy + custom “governing each” + 1-yr bars.</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"sec\">\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:0\">📚 Sources Used (as directed — project materials primary)</h3>\n<p style=\"font-family:Arial;font-size:13.5px\"><b>Primary:</b> DU Case Material <i>LB-105 Family Law-I</i> (Usha Tandon et al., Jan 2023, 303 pp.) — Unit I pp.1–73 (PDF pp.8–81) for all 10 cases + syllabus + rubric; <i>THE HINDU MARRIAGE ACT, 1955-1.pdf</i> (bare act) for Sec 2/3/5/7/8/11/12/17/18; <i>Family Law-1 (2).pdf</i> (Karanveer Kamra summary) for conditions overview; <i>THE PROHIBITION OF CHILD MARRIAGE ACT, 2006.pdf</i> + Lajja extract for PCMA. <b>Supplementary (PYQs):</b> DU Content File LB105 July 2016 (2010–11 papers) + dullbonline PYQ archive 2012–2017 (fetched). <b>Prescribed Material:</b> DU Case Material and Bare Acts.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family:Arial;font-size:13px;color:#555\">Note: Handwritten <i>Family Law.pdf</i> (13 pp. scanned) + <i>Family_Law_Most_Important_Cases</i> (scanned) were visually inspected; content overlapped with above and DU material prevails where conflict (e.g., age consequence, fraud scope). PCMA–HMA anomalies per Usha Tandon article in DU material (pp.52–55) retained verbatim.</p>\n</div>\n\n</div><!-- /wrap -->\n<div class=\"footer\">Crafted for <b>DU LL.B I Term • LB-105 Family Law-I • Unit I</b> • Based strictly on DU Case Material Jan 2023 + HMA Bare Act + Lexis Lectures • For private study use in course of instruction • <b>Tip: Print → Save as PDF → Revise §§4, 7, 8, 9, 10 the night before.</b></div>"
