          "examStrategy": "(1) Ashby v. White: candidate's right to vote was rejected; even though candidate won, voter's constitutional legal right was infringed → nominal damages awarded. (2) Bhim Singh: MLA unlawfully detained to prevent attending assembly → ₹50,000 exemplary damages under Art. 21.",
          "caseMap": "1. Ashby v. White (1703) · 2. Gloucester Grammar School (1410) · 3. Bhim Singh (SC 1985) · 4. Mayor of Bradford v. Pickles (1895).",
          "htmlContent": "<section id=\"revise\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-num\">◆</div><h2>Quick Revision Flowchart — The Whole Topic at a Glance</h2></div>\n      <div class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 900 360\" width=\"900\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Full topic revision flowchart\">\n          <defs><marker id=\"ar3\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"10\" refX=\"7\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L7,3 L0,6 z\" fill=\"#14224a\"/></marker></defs>\n          <rect x=\"10\" y=\"20\" width=\"420\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#14224a\"/>\n          <text x=\"220\" y=\"50\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">WHERE IT CAME FROM</text>\n          <text x=\"220\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#dbe3f5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\">England: Norman Conquest → common law →</text>\n          <text x=\"220\" y=\"94\" fill=\"#dbe3f5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\">FORMS OF ACTION (writs) = specific remedies</text>\n          <text x=\"220\" y=\"113\" fill=\"#dbe3f5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\">→ abolition 1852/1873-75 → judge-made growth</text>\n          <rect x=\"470\" y=\"20\" width=\"420\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#1f3675\"/>\n          <text x=\"680\" y=\"50\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">HOW IT REACHED INDIA</text>\n          <text x=\"680\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#dbe3f5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\">British courts → Mayor’s Courts →</text>\n          <text x=\"680\" y=\"94\" fill=\"#dbe3f5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\">justice, equity &amp; good conscience →</text>\n          <text x=\"680\" y=\"113\" fill=\"#dbe3f5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\">UNCODIFIED &amp; JUDGE-MADE (fragmented statutes)</text>\n          <line x1=\"220\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#14224a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#ar3)\"/>\n          <line x1=\"680\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"680\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#14224a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#ar3)\"/>\n          <rect x=\"10\" y=\"168\" width=\"880\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#c8912b\"/>\n          <text x=\"450\" y=\"196\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">THE NATURE OF A TORT</text>\n          <text x=\"450\" y=\"218\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\">Duty fixed by law · owed to persons generally (in rem) · breach → unliquidated damages (Winfield)</text>\n          <text x=\"450\" y=\"234\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\">Law of TORT (Winfield — general principle)  vs  Law of TORTS (Salmond — pigeon-holes)</text>\n          <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"238\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"255\" stroke=\"#14224a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#ar3)\"/>\n          <rect x=\"10\" y=\"258\" width=\"430\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#eef6f6\" stroke=\"#0f8a8a\"/>\n          <text x=\"225\" y=\"282\" fill=\"#0f8a8a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"700\">CONSTITUENTS</text>\n          <text x=\"225\" y=\"303\" fill=\"#125b5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\">1. Wrongful act  2. Legal damage  3. Remedy</text>\n          <text x=\"225\" y=\"323\" fill=\"#125b5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\">ubi jus ibi remedium</text>\n          <rect x=\"460\" y=\"258\" width=\"430\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#e2f3f3\" stroke=\"#0f8a8a\"/>\n          <text x=\"675\" y=\"282\" fill=\"#0f8a8a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"700\">TWO MAXIMS OF DAMAGE</text>\n          <text x=\"675\" y=\"303\" fill=\"#125b5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\">injury + no damage → actionable (Ashby, Asharfi)</text>\n          <text x=\"675\" y=\"323\" fill=\"#125b5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\">damage + no injury → not actionable (Gloucester, Pickles)</text>\n        </svg>\n        <div class=\"cap\">One-page revision map of Topic 1.</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"hint\"><b>Quick case-type recall:</b><br>\n        · <span class=\"pill g\">Injuria sine damnum</span> — Ashby v. White; Municipal Corpn. Agra v. Asharfi Lal; Bhim Singh.<br>\n        · <span class=\"pill r\">Damnum sine injuria</span> — Gloucester Grammar School; Mayor of Bradford v. Pickles; P. Seetharamayya; Town Area Committee; Mogul Steamship; Acton v. Blundell.<br>\n        · <span class=\"pill n\">Tort &amp; contract — exemption clause</span> — White v. John Warrick.<br>\n        · <span class=\"pill t\">Negligence &amp; remoteness / statutory duty</span> — Rajkot MC v. Manjulben.<br>\n        · <span class=\"pill n\">Motive/malice irrelevant</span> — Pickles; Town Area; Allen v. Flood.\n      </div>\n    </section>"
