          "htmlContent": "<section id=\"s9\">\n  <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"num\">09</div><h2>Sources &amp; How This File Was Built</h2></div>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Primary sources (uploaded project material):</b></p>\n    <ul style=\"margin-left:20px;font-size:13.6px;columns:2;column-gap:26px\">\n      <li><b>LB-303 Company Law (2025 Final)</b> — Faculty of Law, University of Delhi (official case material; the source of the syllabus and all case extracts: Salomon, Bennett Coleman, Daimler, Lee, In re Dinshaw Petit, Associated Rubber, Gilford, Subhra Mukherjee; references: STC, TELCO, Cooper, Meenakshi Mills, Kapila Hingorani).</li>\n      <li><b>Company Law — Class Notes, Dr. Megh Raj</b> (Law Centre-I, DU) — unit-wise notes, theories of personality, grounds of lifting, case capsules, exam-designated questions.</li>\n      <li><b>DU Prescribed Company Law Modules</b> (EBC) — Chapter 1 \"Corporate Personality\" and Chapter 18 \"Kinds of Company\" (definitions, privileges, case footnotes).</li>\n      <li><b>COMPANY LAW by Taxmann</b> — kinds of companies: definitions, private-company privileges, foreign company obligations.</li>\n      <li><b>Company-Law-Exam-Checklist</b> (based on the December 2024 DU paper) — actual PYQ themes Q1 (Art. 19(1)(g)) and Q2 (bonus/subsidiary), statutory anchors.</li>\n      <li><b>COMPANY.md / COMPANY.pdf</b> — distilled summary of the topic (separate entity, citizenship, lifting grounds with case notes).</li>\n      <li><b>Company Law Notes (Renaissance / ASIM)</b> — supplementary framing of the veil doctrine.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p style=\"font-size:13.6px;margin-top:10px\"><b>Cross-verified with:</b> the statutory text of the Companies Act, 2013 (as amended up to 2023–24) and the standard citations. Where a source gives a slightly different rounding (e.g. <i>Associated Rubber</i> cited as (1985) 4 SCC 11 in the syllabus list and as 4 SCC 114 in the casebook), both are recorded.</p>\n    <div class=\"callout info\" style=\"margin-bottom:0\"><div class=\"ic\">⚖️</div><div><b class=\"t\">Disclaimer</b> These are study notes prepared for LL.B. revision from the prescribed materials; not a substitute for the casebook or the statute. Verify section numbers from the latest amended text of the Companies Act, 2013 before the exam. The December 2024 questions are reconstructed from the exam-compiled checklist of the project material.</div></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n</main>\n</div>\n\n<button id=\"toTop\" title=\"Back to top\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑</button>"
