          "anchorId": "revision",
          "htmlContent": "<h2 id=\"app-corr\">Appendix A — IEA 1872 ↔ BSA 2023 Correspondence (used throughout these notes)</h2>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Subject</th><th>IEA 1872</th><th>BSA 2023</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Definitions</td><td>s.3</td><td>s.2</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Evidence of facts in issue &amp; relevant facts</td><td>s.5</td><td>s.3</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Res gestae</td><td>s.6</td><td>s.4</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cause/effect, occasion</td><td>s.7</td><td>s.5</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Motive, preparation, conduct</td><td>s.8</td><td>s.6</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Explanatory/introductory facts</td><td>s.9</td><td>s.7</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Conspiracy</td><td>s.10</td><td>s.8</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Facts inconsistent (alibi)</td><td>s.11</td><td>s.9</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Admissions</td><td>ss.17–23, 31</td><td>ss.15–21, 25</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Confessions (incl. police custody &amp; discovery)</td><td>ss.24–30 (discovery s.27)</td><td>ss.22–24 (discovery s.23)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Dying declaration</td><td>s.32(1)</td><td>s.26(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Expert/third-person opinion</td><td>ss.45–51</td><td>ss.39–45</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Facts not needing proof</td><td>ss.56–58</td><td>ss.51–53</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Oral &amp; documentary evidence; primary/secondary</td><td>ss.59–78 (ss.62–63)</td><td>ss.54–77 (ss.57–58)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Electronic records admissibility</td><td>ss.65A/65B</td><td><b>ss.61–63 (new architecture)</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Exclusion of oral by documentary</td><td>ss.91–92</td><td>ss.94–95</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Legitimacy (birth during marriage)</td><td>s.112</td><td>s.116</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Presumptions (suicide/dowry death)</td><td>ss.113A/113B</td><td>ss.117/118</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Court may presume (illustrations incl. accomplice)</td><td>s.114</td><td>s.119</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Estoppel</td><td>ss.115–117</td><td>ss.121–123</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Competent witnesses / dumb witness</td><td>ss.118/119</td><td>ss.124/125</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Marital communications</td><td>s.122</td><td>s.128</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Advocate's privilege</td><td>ss.126–129</td><td>ss.131–134</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Accomplice</td><td>s.133</td><td>s.138</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Examination/cross/re-examination</td><td>ss.137–139</td><td>ss.142–144</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Hostile witness (questioning own witness)</td><td>s.154</td><td>s.157</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Repeal of IEA</td><td>—</td><td><b>s.170(1)</b></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2 id=\"app-maxims\">Appendix B — Maxims &amp; Doctrines encountered in Unit I</h2>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Maxim / doctrine</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Where used</th></tr>\n<tr><td><span class=\"maxim\">Lex fori</span></td><td>Law of the forum governs evidence</td><td>Topic (j)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><span class=\"maxim\">Contemporanea expositio est optima et fortissima in lege</span></td><td>Contemporaneous exposition is the best in law (rejected as a bar in Desai)</td><td>Desai</td></tr>\n<tr><td><span class=\"maxim\">Nemo moriturus praesumitur mentiri</span></td><td>A dying person is presumed not to lie</td><td>Dying declaration (PYQ 4)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><span class=\"maxim\">Falsus in uno, falsus in omnibus</span></td><td>False in one, false in all — <b>not applicable in India</b> (Bur Singh; Prem Singh)</td><td>Ch.1 notes</td></tr>\n<tr><td><span class=\"maxim\">\"It matters not how you get it\"</span> (R. v. Leatham)</td><td>Illegality → weight/caution, not inadmissibility</td><td>Malkani</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Updating construction (Bennion) / \"ongoing Act\"</td><td>Always-speaking statutes construed for the living present</td><td>Desai; Topic (h)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rule of caution (accomplice)</td><td>Prudence, not law, demands corroboration (Bhuboni Sahu)</td><td>PYQ 7</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Approbate &amp; reprobate (estoppel)</td><td>Cannot blow hot and cold (Sanatan Gauda)</td><td>PYQ 5</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2 id=\"app-allied\">Appendix C — Allied Acts, Rules &amp; Orders map (holistic cross-referencing)</h2>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Provisions touching Unit-I concepts</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Information Technology Act, 2000</td><td>s.2(1)(t)/(i)/(ha) definitions imported via <b>s.2(2) BSA</b>; ss.85A–85B presumptions; s.79A examiner of electronic evidence</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BNS, 2023</td><td>Offence ingredients = facts in issue (s.101 murder, s.61 conspiracy, s.80 dowry death, s.22 insanity); activate BSA presumptions (ss.117–120 BSA)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BNSS, 2023</td><td>Successors of CrPC ss.161/162/164 (statements, confessions, dying declarations), s.273 (presence), ss.284–290 (commissions), s.313 (accused); electronic recording &amp; e-service creating BSA documents</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CPC, 1908</td><td>Order XIV (issues = facts in issue), Order VI/VIII (pleadings gate relevancy via s.3 BSA Explanation), Orders XI/XIII (discovery/documents), XVI (witnesses), XVIII (order of proof), XIX (affidavits), s.11 (res judicata), s.132</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CrPC, 1973 (for pre-1-7-2024 cases)</td><td>ss.161, 162, 164, 273–275, 284–290, 299, 313</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Arbitration &amp; Conciliation Act, 1996</td><td>ss.19, 66 — tribunal outside the Act (matches s.1/s.2(1)(a))</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Others</td><td>Bankers' Books Evidence Act 1891; Commissions of Inquiry Act 1952; Family Courts Act 1984 s.14; Commercial Courts Act 2015 s.14; Contempt of Courts Act 1971</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2 id=\"app-src\">Appendix D — Sources used (uploaded project material)</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>CM_LB201_2025.pdf</b> — DU Faculty of Law case material (primary): course content Unit I(a)–(j); full judgments <i>Prafulla Desai</i> &amp; <i>Malkani</i>; case list.</li>\n  <li><b>BharatiyaSakshyaAdhiniyam2023 / 250882_english_01042024.pdf</b> — BSA 2023 bare act (Gazette): s.2(1)(a)–(l), s.2(2), ss.3, 57–63, 116–170.</li>\n  <li><b>EVIDENCE LATEST.pdf</b> (Dr. K.M. Yadav summary) — history, s.2 repeal material (Hira Advani; Sri Chandra Nandi), falsus in uno, PYQs.</li>\n  <li><b>Asim Evidence.pdf / Evidence .pdf</b> — concept notes, examples, DU PYQs (2003 tape-record; 2005 video-conferencing).</li>\n  <li><b>law of evidence pyp june 2024.pdf</b> — scanned DU LB-201 May–June 2024 paper (OCR-read visually).</li>\n</ul>"
