          "answer": "Model answer (outline). Identify: absolute devise + conditions on sale and letting; law — s.10 TPA (by analogy; wills → s.138 Succession Act); test — substance; Rosher v. Rosher on all fours (one-fifth value; letting at a fraction of rental value); Pearson J.: equivalent to \"during the life of the widow you shall not sell\"; fine/additional rent = circumvention; letting is a mode of disposal; conclusion — both conditions void; S takes absolutely; W has no cause of action; P gets a good title. Contrast: if the option were at market value → partial, valid, W could enjoin a sale to P without first offer (and, P having notice, enforce against P under s.40 limb 2/SRA s.19(b)).",
