          "question": "DU Semester Examination Question 4",
          "answer": "Model answer (outline). Facts (1926 Society; Bye-laws 7 and 21; land acquired 1928 under LA Act s.41; Respondent 2 inherited, sought to sell Plot 7 to a builders' association; authorities and High Court held bye-law opposed to public policy and hit by s.10). Issues. Arguments (Sorabjee — Art. 19(1)(c), Art. 29, partial restraint, Part III applies to State action; Bobde — s.4 public policy, s.10 TPA, s.14/s.24). Reasoning: s.24 open membership subject to bye-laws; public policy not to be judicially expanded ( Gherulal Parakh ); legislature's task; s.10 applies only to a restraint imposed in a transfer — here inheritance with limitations (s.31), voluntary acceptance of bye-laws and s.30; membership transfer outside s.10; even otherwise a partial restraint (transfer to anyone qualified) — valid like restraints in family settlements/partitions ( Muhammad Raza ; Gummanna Shetty ); Art. 300-A not infringed. Result. Critical note (exclusionary housing; Art. 15(2) debate; Court's own call for legislation). Conclusion: statement correct as the ratio; but s.10 would still apply to a restraint inserted in a private sale deed.",
