          "answer": "Points. (a) Lease — lessor's reversionary interest; s.108(j), 111(g), 114-A, rent-control eviction grounds; married woman not Hindu/Muslim/Buddhist — restraint on anticipation, only during marriage, historical reason (stridhan, Muslim wife's capacity), English abolition 1949. (b) Forfeiture on insolvency/attempted alienation void; interest \"reserved or given\"; lease exception; relation to ss.28, 30, 31, 32; insolvency law — property vests in assignee/RP; example. (c) Condition qualifies a defined estate; limitation marks its duration (\"until\", \"so long as\"); English determinable-fee loophole closed by \"or limitation\" in ss.10 and 12; condition precedent (s.26 substantial compliance) v. subsequent (s.29 strict). (d) Muhammad Raza — compromise is a contract as to terms of taking, not a conveyance; equity favours family arrangements; partial restraints therein binding; Zoroastrian para 42; Gummanna Shetty ; Kale v. DDC on validity/registration of family settlements.",
