          "answer": "Model answer (outline). Definition (Lewis, via Ram Baran Prasad ); rationale ( Kempraj quotation; Capsule objects); text of s.14; five essentials (Capsule) — transfer; ultimate unborn beneficiary with absolute interest (s.13); prior life interests in living persons; beneficiary in existence at end of last life; vesting ≤ minority. Period: lives in being + (gestation) + minority (18 — Majority Act); vesting must not be capable of being delayed beyond it; illustrations (18 valid, 25 void, 10 valid). Possible-events test ( Ram Newaz ). England: lives in being + 21 years in gross; 1964 Act (wait and see, 80 years), 2009 Act (125 years); India retains strict rule. Effect: interest void in toto; s.16 consequences; s.15 class gifts. Exceptions/limits: s.18 public benefit; personal covenants/contracts/pre-emption ( Ram Baran Prasad ); lease renewal/lease in perpetuity ( Kempraj ); vested interests with postponed enjoyment (s.19 Expl.); charges; Muslim/Hindu personal-law and statutory contexts; wills — s.114 ISA.",
