          "question": "DU Semester Examination Question 5",
          "answer": "Points. (a) Meaning of class; pre-1929 whole-class failure v. post-1929 partial failure; examples (children who attain 25 — all fail; children of B and of unborn C — only C's fail); s.22; ISA s.115 contrast. (b) Dependent limitations; illustration to s.13 (A's second son); Ram Newaz (vendee's interest); contrast ss.27 and 30; independent limitations survive; ISA s.116. (c) Thellusson Act background; longer of transferor's life or 18 years; void only as to excess; disposal thereafter; three exceptions (debts, portions, preservation); ISA s.117; example. (d) Public benefit — religion, knowledge, commerce, health, safety, other objects beneficial to mankind; exempt from ss.14, 16, 17 (not s.13); endowments, wakfs, trusts; Pemsel heads; Income-tax s.2(15) analogy.",
