          "answer": "Points. (i) C's remainder vested (B's death certain; Expl. (ii)) — not defeated by C's death; C's heirs take on B's death. (ii) Contingent on marriage to D; B's death unmarried makes the event impossible → interest fails; property remains with A (s.21; Capsule). (iii) Vested — Exception to s.21 (income applied for B's benefit); if B dies at 18 his heirs take. (iv) B vested subject to divestment (Expl. (iv); s.28); C contingent; if A dies first, B's interest becomes indefeasible; if B dies first, C's vests (s.29 strict compliance).",
