          "answer": "Answer. Not hit. Under the Explanation to s.52 pendency commences only on presentation of the plaint in a court of competent jurisdiction — 25 January. On 15 January no suit was pending in such a court ( Govinda Pillai Gopala Pillai v. Aiyyappan Krishnan , Ker 1957, following Gouri Dutt and Nathusingh , and holding Ma Than (Rang 1927) no longer good law after the 1929 amendment; analogy with s.14 Limitation Act). C's knowledge is irrelevant to s.52 because the doctrine rests on necessity, not notice — knowledge neither brings a case within s.52 nor takes it out ( G.T. Girish ). A's remedies: implead C (O.I r.10) and seek relief against him on the merits of title; the gift being gratuitous, s.53 may be pleaded if made to defeat A as a creditor, and s.41 cannot protect a donee. Result: gift valid so far as s.52 is concerned.",
