          "answer": "Points. (a) Secret arrangement, no real contest, to defeat a third party — s.52 inapplicable (1929 words \"which is not collusive\"; Capsule A–B–D example); distinguish fraudulent-but-contested suit (covered) and compromise (covered unless collusive). (b) Explanation: plaint in competent court → final decree + complete satisfaction / execution time-barred; wrong court ( Govinda Pillai ), rejected plaint, appeals and SLP ( Dalip Kaur ), execution and restitution. (c) Voluntary — sale, mortgage, lease, gift, exchange, charge, compromise ( Supreme General Films ); involuntary — court sales, insolvency; both subject to the lis; court-authorised transfers exempt. (d) Not void; valid inter partes; subject to decree; transferee bound regardless of notice; cannot obstruct execution (O.XXI r.102); restitution (s.144); may be impleaded (O.XXII r.10); helps only the party who succeeds ( G.T. Girish ).",
