          "answer": "Outline. s.58(a) definition; four essentials (parties; transfer of an interest; specific immovable property; purpose of security for loan/debt/pecuniary engagement) with explanation; six kinds (ss.58(b)–(g)) — text, elements, illustration, remedy (use Part 3 and the comparative table): simple (no possession, personal covenant, sale through court); conditional sale (ostensible sale; three conditions; 1929 proviso — same document; foreclosure only; sale v. mortgage tests — Chunchun Jha ); usufructuary (possession; usufruct in lieu of interest/principal; no personal liability; no sale/foreclosure; s.62); English (absolute transfer with proviso; certain date; personal covenant; sale; s.69); deposit of title deeds (notified towns; deposit + intent; no writing; s.96 — sale); anomalous (combinations; s.98; Pomal Kanji ). Mode of execution — s.59. Conclude with s.67's scheme of remedies and the co-extensive nature of the rights ( Ganga Dhar ).",
