          "question": "DU Semester Examination Question 5",
          "answer": "Outline. s.58(a) v. s.100 (text); the Part 10.1 table — transfer of interest v. none; act of parties only v. also operation of law; formalities; personal liability; remedies (sale only for charge; provisions of simple mortgage apply); kinds; redemption/clog; limitation. Illustrations: vendor's charge s.55(4)(b); maintenance charge ( Rajesh Kanta Roy compromise decree); partition-money charge. Answer the second part: No — the last limb of s.100 (1929) provides that \"no charge shall be enforced against any property in the hands of a person to whom such property has been transferred for consideration and without notice of the charge\", save where a law expressly provides otherwise (e.g., statutory charges for land revenue/tax which bind all); contrast a mortgage which, being an interest in the property, binds transferees regardless of notice (registration itself being notice — s.3 Expl. I).",
