          "answer": "Q.5 (Short notes — any two). (a) Mode of making a gift (s.123); (b) Onerous gift; (c) Universal donee; (d) Gift of future property and gift to several donees; (e) Pardanashin donor. Model answer (outline). (a) Immovable: registered instrument (s.17(1)(a) Registration Act; no value threshold) signed by/for donor, attested by ≥2 witnesses (s.3 definition of \"attested\"; scribe with animus; proof under s.68 Evidence Act); delivery of possession neither necessary nor sufficient; registration may follow donor's death (s.47); movable: instrument or delivery as goods sold (s.33 SOGA); Muslim hiba exempt (s.129). (b) s.127 — single transfer of several things, one burdened: accept all or nothing (Illustration (a) shares in X and Y); separate independent transfers: may pick (Illustration (b)); minor donee not bound until he retains after majority with knowledge; maxim qui sentit commodum . (c) s.128 — gift of whole property makes donee personally liable for donor's debts and liabilities existing at the date of gift up to the value of the property; protects creditors; Kartari donor gave everything — evidence of unconscionability. (d) s.124 — void as to future property (severable); s.125 — non-accepting donee's share remains with donor. (e) Farid-un-nisa , Chinta Dasya , Kartari — burden on person relying on the deed to prove it was explained and understood; independent advice; extends to illiterate/ignorant women and, today, illiterate/aged persons; interacts with s.16(3) Contract Act and s.111 Evidence Act.",
