          "name": "APP Appendices, Checklists and Sources Six appendices for revision: the cases, the instruments, the master grid of the zones, the glossary, an index of every UNCLOS article used, and a note on materials and method — followed by an appendix that decodes the syllabus image itself, including the two entries the teacher highlighted and the handwritten annotations. Appendix A · Table of cases (Topic 5) Table 5.32 · Cases and decisions cited in these notes Case Citation Subject Where Anglo-Norwegian Fisheries (United Kingdom v. Norway) ICJ Rep. 1951, p. 116 — case 30 of the syllabus Straight baselines; bays; burden of proof; persistent objector §5.1.1; case 30 Corfu Channel (United Kingdom v. Albania) ICJ Rep. 1949, p. 4 — case 31 Straits used for international navigation; innocent passage of warships; duty to warn; satisfaction; compensation §5.1.1; case 31 North Sea Continental Shelf (Federal Republic of Germany v. Denmark; Federal Republic of Germany v. Netherlands) ICJ Rep. 1969, p. 3 — case 32 Equitable principles; equidistance not customary; natural prolongation; negotiated settlement §5.2; case 32 Continental Shelf (Tunisia/Libyan Arab Jamahiriya) ICJ Rep. 1982, p. 17 — case 33 Equity infra legem ; relevant circumstances; half-effect for islands; economic arguments excluded §5.2; case 33 Republic of Italy v. Union of India (2013) 4 SCC 721 — case 34 (highlighted in the syllabus) Jurisdiction over the Enrica Lexie incident; Union's competence; Article 97; immunity; special court §5.2; case 34 Bay of Bengal Maritime Boundary Arbitration (Bangladesh v. India) PCA, Award of 7 July 2014 — case 35 Concavity and cut-off; low-tide elevations; shelf beyond 200 nm; grey area §5.2; case 35 Maritime Delimitation in the Indian Ocean (Somalia v. Kenya) ICJ Rep. 2021 (preliminary objections 2017) — case 36 Acquiescence; base points; three-stage method; Articles 74(3)/83(3); no reparation §5.2; case 36 Delimitation of the Maritime Boundary in the Bay of Bengal (Bangladesh/Myanmar) ITLOS Case No. 16, Judgment of 14 March 2012 The first delimitation of the shelf beyond 200 nm; cut-off; no effect for St Martin's Island in the EEZ §5.2; cases 35 and 36 Dispute concerning delimitation of the maritime boundary between Ghana and Côte d'Ivoire ITLOS Special Chamber, Case No. 23, Judgment of 23 September 2017 Articles 74(3)/83(3); provisional arrangements; tacit agreement rejected §5.2 G Dispute concerning delimitation of the maritime boundary between Mauritius and Maldives in the Indian Ocean ITLOS Special Chamber, Case No. 28, Judgment of 28 January 2023 (preliminary objections 2021) Delimitation; Chagos sovereignty not determined; equidistance §5.2; §5.6 D Responsibilities and Obligations of States Sponsoring Persons and Entities with respect to Activities in the Area (Advisory Opinion) Seabed Disputes Chamber, Case No. 17, 1 February 2011 Sponsoring States; due diligence; precautionary approach; environmental impact assessment; erga omnes obligations §5.3 G; §5.4 D Request for an Advisory Opinion submitted by the Sub-Regional Fisheries Commission ITLOS Case No. 21, 2 April 2015 Flag-State obligations for IUU fishing; advisory jurisdiction under Annex VI, art. 21 §5.6 D Request for an Advisory Opinion on Climate Change and International Law (COSIS) ITLOS Case No. 31, 21 May 2024 Greenhouse gases as marine pollution; stringent due diligence; precautionary approach §5.1.6 E; §5.6 D The M/V \"Saiga\" (No. 1) ; The M/V \"Saiga\" (No. 2) ITLOS Cases Nos. 1 and 2 (1997; 1999) Prompt release and bond; bunkering; use of force; Article 73 §5.1.4; §5.6 D \"Camouco\" ; \"Monte Confurco\" ; \"Grand Prince\" ; \"Volga\" ; \"Juno Trader\" ; \"Hoshinmaru\" ; \"Tomimaru\" ITLOS, 2000–2007 Prompt release; reasonableness of the bond; proof of nationality §5.6 D \"ARA Libertad\" (Argentina v. Ghana) ITLOS Case No. 20, Order of 15 December 2012 Immunity of warships; provisional measures §5.6 D \"Arctic Sunrise\" (Netherlands v. Russian Federation) ITLOS Case No. 22, Order of 22 November 2013; Annex VII Award of 14 August 2015 Provisional measures pending arbitration; non-appearance; freedom of navigation in the EEZ §5.6 D \"Enrica Lexie\" (Italy v. India) ITLOS Case No. 24, Order of 24 August 2015; PCA Award of 21 May 2020; Supreme Court of India, 15 June 2021 Suspension of proceedings; immunity; Articles 87/90; compensation; quashing under Article 142 §5.2; case 34 \"M/V Virginia G\" (Panama v. Guinea-Bissau) ITLOS Case No. 19, Judgment of 14 April 2014 Bunkering in the EEZ; coastal-State competence; manner of enforcement; compensation §5.1.4; §5.6 D M/T \"Norstar\" (Panama v. Italy) ITLOS Case No. 25, Judgment of 10 April 2019 Freedom of navigation on the high seas; limits of criminal jurisdiction over foreign ships §5.6 D In re Piracy Jure Gentium [1934] A.C. 586 (P.C.) Piracy; attempt sufficient; actual robbery not necessary §5.1.5; PYQ Answer 5 The Lotus (France v. Turkey) P.C.I.J., Series A, No. 10 (1927) Flag-State jurisdiction on the high seas; the \"effects\" doctrine; now Article 97 §5.1.5 Nottebohm (Liechtenstein v. Guatemala) ICJ Rep. 1955, p. 4 Nationality and the genuine link — the analogy used in the law of the sea §5.1.5 Republic of Italy v. Union of India (Supreme Court, subsequent stages) W.P. (C) No. 135 of 2012 and connected matters; order of 15 June 2021 Quashing of proceedings; compensation; closure of the case case 34 (postscript) Appendix B · Table of instruments",
