          "question": "1. Facts and the question The General Assembly, concerned at the deadlock in the Conference on Disarmament and acting under Article 96(1) of the Charter, requested the Court to give an advisory opinion on the question: &ldquo;Is the threat or use of nuclear weapons in any circumstance permitted under international law?&rdquo; The Court heard statements from forty-five States and received written statements from others. In parallel, the World Health Organization had asked its own question, which the Court declined to answer for want of jurisdiction (the question did not arise within the scope of the WHO's activities).",
