          "question": "3. The questions before the Court May a court of the United States, at the suit of private claimants who allege that their vessel was taken from them contrary to the law of nations and never condemned by any competent prize court, exercise jurisdiction over that vessel when she is now a public armed ship in the service of a foreign sovereign at peace with the United States, and is present in an American port? If the vessel is exempt from the jurisdiction, by what means may that fact be brought before the court — in particular, is the suggestion of the Attorney of the United States a proper mode of doing so, when the foreign sovereign is not himself before the court and no claimant appears?",
