          "question": "3. The questions before the Court The Court framed its task in two steps, in terms which organise every answer on this head: \"First, it must determine how far, legally, the acts in question may be regarded as imputable to the Iranian State. Secondly, it must consider their compatibility or incompatibility with the obligations of Iran under treaties in force or under any other rules of international law that may be applicable\" (paragraph 56). The events, it said, \"fall into two phases which it will be convenient to examine separately.\"",
