          "file": "sem 3/Constitution/Topic3-UnionAndStateExecutives-LB301-DU-Notes.html",
          "anchorId": "c-kapur",
          "facts": "Jayalalithaa had been convicted and sentenced to imprisonment for not less than two years in corruption cases (TANSI and others); her conviction was not stayed — only the sentence was suspended (she was on bail). Her nomination for election was rejected under s. 8(3) of the Representation of the People Act, 1951 (disqualification for conviction + sentence ≥ 2 years). Nevertheless, on her party's (AIADMK's) overwhelming electoral victory, she was appointed Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu on 14-5-2001 . The appointment was challenged by way of quo warranto . The High Court/quashing proceedings led to the Constitution Bench.",
