          "facts": "Facts TISCO manufactured iron and steel at Jamshedpur (Bihar) and sold to buyers all over India, dispatching goods on its own railway receipts (TISCO as consignee, freight paid by it; receipts sent to branches/banks to be released on payment). Under the Bihar Sales Tax Act, 1947 (Bihar Act 19 of 1947), s. 4(1) read with s. 2(g) and the second proviso inserted by the Bihar (Amendment) Act 6 of 1949 , the Sales Tax Officer disallowed TISCO’s deductions for sales made/ goods delivered & consumed outside Bihar and added the sales-tax realisations of ₹13,66,496 (first period) and ₹22,37,919 (second period) to the taxable turnover — assessing TISCO to ₹15,31,374-5-9 and ₹28,30,458-6-9 respectively. The Commissioner of Sales Tax (Chota Nagpur) dismissed TISCO’s appeals; the Patna High Court upheld the Act’s validity but framed references (including on whether tax collected from customers as such formed part of the taxable turnover). The matter reached the Supreme Court.",
