          "anchorId": "c69",
          "facts": "Facts. The Janata Party swept the March 1977 Lok Sabha elections, defeating the Congress across the country. On 18-4-1977 , the Union Home Minister, Shri Charan Singh, addressed letters to the Chief Ministers of the six Congress-ruled States — Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Punjab, Bihar, Himachal Pradesh and Orissa (Odisha) — advising them to dissolve their Legislative Assemblies and seek a fresh mandate; the Union indicated that if the advice was not followed, action under Art 356 (and, implicitly, Art 365 — non-compliance with directions) might follow. The six States filed suits under Art 131 (plus connected writ petitions) seeking declarations that such an invocation would be unconstitutional and mala fide and injunctions restraining recourse to Art 356 on that sole ground.",
