          "content": "id=\"s-rev\"> §11 Rapid-Revision Kit LAST-15-MINUTE PAGE Diagram 9 — Master map of Topic 7 (the whole chapter on one screen) ⚡ Article flash-cards 245(1): extent of laws (Parliament — whole/any part; States — whole/any part); extraterritorial legislation OK with nexus . 245(2): extraterritorial laws for Parts A/B/C — sole exception (G.V.K.: “for India” = benefit-to-India, real not fanciful). 246: (1) List I exclusive (notwithstanding); (2) List III concurrent subject to (1); (3) List II exclusive subject to (1),(2); (4) any matter for non-State territory = UT route. 247: additional courts for Union laws. 248+Entry 97: residue incl. taxes not in either List — one negative question (Dhillon). 249: Rajya Sabha ⅔ → specified State matter, 1 year (never used). 250: Art 352 emergency → whole State List, ends +6 months (251 makes State law inoperative meanwhile). 252: ≥2 States’ request → Union law (State assemblies can’t repeal). 253: treaties/conventions → any law for whole of India, “notwithstanding … this Chapter”. 254(1): State law repugnant to Parliament law (competent) or existing concurrent law → Union prevails “whether passed before or after”; State void to extent. 254(2): reserved + President’s assent → State law prevails over earlier Union law in that State; proviso = Parliament’s add/amend/varies/repeals power; Explanation includes previously passed Acts. 255: procedural defects saved. 356: 246(4)’s twin for breakdown — (1) satisfaction + HC proviso; (3) 2-month approval; ",
