          "htmlContent": "<section class=\"card\" id=\"diagrams\">\n<h2>13. Diagrams &amp; Flowcharts</h2>\n<h3>13.1 The <i>Prakash Singh</i> reform architecture (one view)</h3>\n<div class=\"flow\">\n<div class=\"fbox dark\">PRAKASH SINGH v. UOI (2006) — Arts. 32 + 142 • “till legislation”</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"cols\">\n<div class=\"fbox green\">🛡️ AUTONOMY LIMB<br>SSC (policy shield) → DGP + field tenures → PEB (transfers) → NSC (CPO chiefs)</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\">⚖️ ACCOUNTABILITY LIMB<br>District PCA (≤ DySP) + State PCA (≥ SP) → serious misconduct → binding action</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\">🔬 PROFESSIONALISM LIMB — Separation of investigation from law &amp; order (10L+ cities first)</div>\n</div>\n<h3>13.2 DGP appointment flowchart (Directive 2 + 2018/19 orders)</h3>\n<div class=\"flow\">\n<div class=\"fbox\">State sends proposal to UPSC <b>3 months before</b> retirement (2018) — NO acting DGPs</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\">UPSC empanels senior-most officers → panel of 3</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\">State appoints <b>on merit</b> from panel; appointee needs <b>≥ 6 months residual service</b> (2019)</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"fbox green\">2-YEAR TENURE irrespective of superannuation → removable only via SSC + AIS/conviction/incapacity (<i>Senkumar</i>: objective material needed)</div>\n</div>\n<h3>13.3 Complaints Authority tree (Directive 6)</h3>\n<div class=\"flow\">\n<div class=\"fbox dark\">Complaint of SERIOUS MISCONDUCT (custodial death / grievous hurt / rape / extortion)</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"cols\">\n<div class=\"fbox\">Against ≤ DySP → <b>DISTRICT PCA</b><br>Chair: Retd. District Judge</div>\n<div class=\"fbox\">Against ≥ SP → <b>STATE PCA</b><br>Chair: Retd. HC/SC Judge</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"farrow\">▼</div>\n<div class=\"fbox green\">Inquiry → Recommendations BINDING on Government (members from NHRC/Lok Ayukta/PSC panels)</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"card\" id=\"revise\">\n<h2>14. One-Page Rapid Revision ⚡</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><b>1861</b> = control model • <b>NPC 1977–81</b> = 8 reports, SSC idea • <b>Ribeiro 1998–99</b> = endorses NPC • <b>Padmanabhaiah 2000</b> = 240 recs • <b>Malimath 2003</b> = 158 recs • <b>49 MHA recs 2005</b> = 5 heads • <b>Model Police Act 30-10-2006</b>.</li>\n<li><b><i>Prakash Singh</i> 22-9-2006</b> (Sabharwal C.J.): <b>7 directives</b> — SSC, DGP tenure, field tenure, separation, PEB, PCA, NSC; <b>Art. 32+142</b>; comply by <b>31-12-2006</b>.</li>\n<li><b>11-1-2007</b> = (2)(3)(5) self-executory • <b>K.T. Thomas 16-5-2008</b> = monitoring • <b>3-7-2018</b> = no acting DGPs • <b>13-3-2019</b> = 6-month residual tenure.</li>\n<li><b><i>Senkumar</i> 24-4-2017</b> (Lokur J.): Kerala DGP reinstated; s. 97(2)(e) needs <b>objective material</b>; no <b>scapegoating</b>.</li>\n<li><b>Custodial chain:</b> <i>Joginder Kumar → D.K. Basu</i> (11) <i>→ Nilabati</i> (₹1.5L) <i>→ Arnesh Kumar</i> (s. 35 BNSS) • <b>BNSS:</b> arrest 35 • FIR 173 • investigation 175–176 • remand 187 • report 193.</li>\n<li><b>PYQ 2017 Q8(a)</b> = 7 directives + enforcement + critique + “skeleton/flesh” conclusion. <b>Federal caveat:</b> Police = State subject → Centre persuades, Court monitors.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</main>"
