          "htmlContent": "id=\"s10\"><span class=\"snum\">10</span><span class=\"stxt\"><small>Revision</small>Master tables, case index and the last-hour sheet</span></h2>\n\n<h3 id=\"s10-1\"><span class=\"tick\">◆</span>10.1 The five heads at a glance</h3>\n\n<div class=\"tw\">\n<table>\n<caption>Everything about s. 14 in one table</caption>\n<thead><tr><th style=\"width:11%\">Head</th><th style=\"width:11%\">Charge</th><th style=\"width:13%\">Computation</th><th style=\"width:22%\">Deductions</th><th style=\"width:15%\">Basis of charge</th><th>Landmark case</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">A · Salaries</td><td>s. 15</td><td>ss. 16–17</td><td>Three only: standard deduction, entertainment allowance (Govt.), professional tax</td><td>Due or paid, whichever is earlier</td><td><em>Ram Pershad</em>; <em>L.W. Russel</em></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">B · Interest on securities</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"background:#efe9dc\"><strong>Omitted by the Finance Act, 1988 w.e.f. 1-4-1989</strong> — such interest is now business income or other-sources income (§1.4)</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">C · House property</td><td>s. 22</td><td>ss. 23–27</td><td>Two: 30% of NAV (s. 24(a)); interest (s. 24(b))</td><td>Annual value — notional where not let</td><td><em>Biman Behari Shaw</em>; <em>East India Housing</em>; <em>Jodhamal Kuthiala</em></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">D · Business or profession</td><td>s. 28</td><td>ss. 29–44</td><td>The whole code, ss. 30–37, read with the disallowances in ss. 40–43B</td><td>Real profits computed on commercial principles, subject to the statute</td><td><em>B.D. Bharucha</em>; <em>Mysore Sugar</em>; <em>Empire Jute</em>; <em>L.B. Sugar</em>; <em>Bikaner Gypsums</em>; <em>General Insurance</em></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">E · Capital gains</td><td>s. 45</td><td>ss. 46–55</td><td>Cost of acquisition, cost of improvement, transfer expenses; exemptions ss. 54–54GB</td><td>Year of transfer; realised gain</td><td><em>N. Bagavathy Ammal</em></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">F · Other sources</td><td>s. 56</td><td>ss. 57–59</td><td>s. 57 — a closed list plus s. 57(iii)</td><td>Receipt or accrual, as the item requires</td><td><em>Rajendra Prasad Moody</em></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 id=\"s10-2\"><span class=\"tick\">◆</span>10.2 Case index — all fifteen, with the ratio in one line</h3>\n\n<div class=\"tw\">\n<table class=\"compact\">\n<caption>The prescribed cases (nos. 13–27) in order</caption>\n<thead><tr><th style=\"width:5%\">No.</th><th style=\"width:24%\">Case</th><th style=\"width:8%\">Reader pp.</th><th style=\"width:12%\">Head</th><th>Ratio in one line</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">13</td><td><em>Ram Pershad v. CIT</em>, (1972) 2 SCC 696</td><td>84–89</td><td>A</td><td>A managing director is an employee in that capacity; the control test is not universal; salary \"due\" is taxable though unpaid, and a waiver after accrual is only an application of income.</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">14</td><td><em>CIT v. L.W. Russel</em>, AIR 1965 SC 49</td><td>90–94</td><td>A</td><td>A contingent right to an annuity is not a perquisite; nothing is \"paid, due or allowed\" until the benefit vests.</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">15</td><td><em>CIT, W.B. v. Biman Behari Shaw Shebait</em>, 68 ITR 815</td><td>95–97</td><td>C</td><td>House-property income is notional: what the property \"might reasonably be expected to let\" for; a covenant against letting reduces but does not eliminate the annual value.</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">16</td><td><em>East India Housing &amp; Land Development Trust v. CIT</em>, 42 ITR 49</td><td>98–99</td><td>C</td><td>The heads are mutually exclusive; a receipt within a specific head cannot be taxed under another head merely because it is indirectly covered; bare letting is s. 22 even for a company.</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"k\">17</td><td><em>R.B. Jodhamal Kuthiala v. CIT</em>, AIR 1972 SC 126</td><td>100–106</td><td>C</td><td>The \"owner\" is the person who can exercise the rights of an owner in his own right and is entitled to the income; vesting in a Custodian"
